The upstream/ directory contains the third-party packages that libiw4x
builds from source. Each of them is licensed under its own terms, which the
files of the package state:

upstream/libz/

  The zlib compression library, licensed under the zlib license (see
  upstream/libz/LICENSE). The package comes from the build2 packaging of
  zlib:

  https://git.build2.org/cgit/packaging/zlib/

upstream/libcurl/

  The libcurl URL transfer library, licensed under the curl license, an
  MIT/X derivative (see upstream/libcurl/COPYING). The package comes from
  the build2 packaging of curl, with its build configuration reduced to the
  parts of the library that libiw4x uses:

  https://git.build2.org/cgit/packaging/curl/

upstream/libquill/

  The Quill logging library, licensed under the MIT license, which the
  header of each of its source files states. It bundles the {fmt}
  formatting library in upstream/libquill/include/quill/bundled/fmt/,
  licensed under the MIT license with the optional exception for object
  code (see the header of format.h in that directory). The package comes
  from the build2 packaging of Quill:

  https://github.com/build2-packaging/quill
